# Step 001 — IMPLEMENT

```step
anchor: IMPLEMENT
touches: [OpticalConstructor.Domain, OpticalConstructor.TestWindows, OpticalConstructor.Tests]
depends_on: []
```

**How to implement.** In Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs make the sample stack DATA: add SampleLayer (materialId + thickness : Thickness; materialId stays a string until step 2 elevates it), PeriodGroup (cell : SampleLayer list, count : int), StackItem = SingleLayer of SampleLayer | Repeated of PeriodGroup, and SampleStructure (films : StackItem list, substrate : SampleLayer option, lower : material-id option where None = vacuum) with a pure expansion member mirroring RepeatBuilder.expand (OpticalConstructor.Ui/RepeatBuilder.fs:24). Replace Sample.materialId + Sample.thickness (ElementId.fs:45-49) with structure : SampleStructure, keeping substrate : SubstrateKind (ElementId.fs:35) as the geometry facet; re-seed all 11 samples in Library.seedEntries (ElementId.fs:189) structurally - the quarter-wave stack becomes Repeated 20x[glass quarter-wave; vacuum quarter-wave] plus one trailing glass layer, the EUV stack Repeated 100x[Mo; Si], langasite-on-silicon becomes films [langasite] with lower = silicon. Add the missing built-ins to MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries (MaterialLibrary.fs:79): euv-molybdenum / euv-silicon over OpticalProperties.euvMolybdenum / euvSilicon (OpticalProperties/Standard.fs:110-111) and active-crystal over OpticalProperties.planarCrystal with n11 2.315, n33 2.226, rho12 1.5e-6 (the constants currently at Propagation.fs:115-119). In Propagation.fs delete the sample.id string branching of sampleToSystem (Propagation.fs:139-141,157,172,180) and the propertiesOf glass-fallback map (Propagation.fs:104-111): add resolveSampleMaterials : MaterialLibrary -> Sample -> Result<ResolvedSample, MaterialError> resolving every referenced material to its OpticalPropertiesWithDisp (an unknown id is a typed Error, never a fallback), rebuild sampleToSystem as a total ResolvedSample -> WaveLength -> OpticalSystem over the expanded structure (no rotation yet - step 20 adds it), and re-point sampleMueller and the sweep builders at ResolvedSample; hosts resolve once per run and surface the error as a message.

**Acceptance.** After the change, every seeded sample's structurally-built OpticalSystem at a reference wavelength MUST equal the previously hand-built system (film count, substrate, tensors), and resolving a sample that names an unknown material MUST return a typed Error - with the solution building and existing tests green.
